<ContentLayout
  title="About Fix The Speaker: Free Phone Speaker Cleaner"
  description="Fix The Speaker is a free, browser-based phone speaker cleaner that uses sound to eject water and loosen dust. Learn how and why it was built."
  heading="About Fix The Speaker"
  eyebrow="About"
>
  <p>
    Fix The Speaker is a free micro-tool that does one thing well: it uses sound to clear a phone speaker grille. Play a
    tone, hold the phone speaker-down, and trapped water is pushed out in about a minute. A second mode loosens dust
    and lint, and a third checks that both channels are working.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Almost every phone sounds muffled at some point, usually after rain, a shower or a spilled drink. The fix is
    simple physics, yet most people are told to bury their phone in rice or wait it out. We wanted a tool that is honest
    about what it can do, works instantly on any device, and does not bury the button under ads and clutter.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Water Eject</strong> plays a 165 Hz pulsing sine wave that moves the diaphragm in large strokes, pushing droplets out through the grille.</li>
    <li><strong>Dust Cleaner</strong> sweeps between 10 kHz and 15 kHz to vibrate loose particles so they can be brushed off.</li>
    <li><strong>Speaker Test</strong> plays a tone through the left channel, the right channel and then both, so you can hear which side needs attention.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Every tone is generated in your browser with the Web Audio API. Nothing is downloaded, nothing is recorded and the
    tool never asks for microphone access.
  </p>

  <h2>What it will not do</h2>
  <p>
    This tool ejects water from the speaker grille. It does not repair internal hardware damage. If your phone was
    submerged, shows a liquid warning in the charging port, or still crackles after several dry cycles, have it inspected
    by a professional.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
